  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kayunga Nile Coffee Processing Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sector: Agriculture. Crops Coffee.Beneficiaries: 507 smallholder farmers of whom 147 are women...Project funds will be used to procure wet coffee cherry processing equipment to process red ripe coffee cherries into FAQ beans that fetch a higher price on the market. Some project funds will be used to provide working capital for procurement of inputs and to pay farmers when they deliver their coffee to the cooperative. Other project funds will be used to train farmers in improved coffee management techniques and post-harvest handling as well as to strengthen the organizations management capacity..</narrative>
  </description>
